"Module 3: Assigning lessons – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042194831)\nciteturn1027view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1025view5\",\"id\":30}); Redirected to URL: https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042194831-Module-3-Assigning-lessons; Total lines: 124\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # Module 3: Assigning lessons\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:45\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: 【13†iframe†www.youtube-nocookie.com】\nL24: \nL25: With Teacher Tools, you can assign lessons to students and view their progress. Teachers can assign lessons to the whole class, an individual student, or a small group, making it easy to meet a wide variety of learning needs. Continue reading below to learn...\nL26: \nL27:   * 【14†How to browse for lessons】\nL28:   * 【15†How to send assignments to students】\nL29:   * 【16†How to manage existing assignments】\nL30: 【17†Image: AssignDialog.png】\nL31: ## How to browse for lessons\nL32: \nL33: There are three easy ways to find lessons: browse the Library tabs (Letters, Reading, etc.); 【18†assign from the Class Report】; or 【19†search by standard from the Search tab】. Tap directly on an assignment to preview the lesson, select students, and set the date that students will receive the assignment.\nL34: #### 1. Browse the Library\nL35: \nL36: Teachers have access to every Pre-K—2nd grade lesson in Khan Academy Kids in the Library. Tap the tabs across the top of the screen—Letters, Reading, Math, Logic+, Books, and Videos—to find lessons for each letter of the alphabet, for numbers 1-20+, patterning, sight words, phonemes, shapes, word problems, and more. Tap directly on any lesson thumbnail to assign.\nL37: \nL38: 【20†Image: Assign_Library.png】\nL39: To access the full range of content, be sure to adjust the dropdown menu as needed. The dropdown menu will allow you to see lessons across grade levels. You'll find it on the following tabs: Reading, Math, Logic+, and Videos.\nL40: \nL41: 【21†Image: Library_Dropdown.png】\nL42: After adjusting the grade level, be sure to scroll down to view all sections. There is a heading for each section (e.g., Print Concepts, Phonological Awareness, Prefixes) to guide you through the Library. If you haven’t found what you’re looking for, keep scrolling! Or, try our other methods for finding lessons to assign.\nL43: \nL44: 【22†Image: KhanKids_G2E_EmailHowToTeacher__1_.gif】\nL45: Lessons in the Library are labeled according to their level: Main, Practice 1, Practice 2, and Basic. Start by assigning the Main lesson, and then assign the Basic version to students who need extra support, and Practice lessons to students who are ready for a challenge.\nL46: Main All students should start here.  | Practice 1 Assign after mastering the Main lesson.  | Practice 2 Assign after mastering the Practice 1 lesson.  | Basic Assign if students need support.\nL47: 【23†Image: Screen_Shot_2021-07-06_at_6.20.41_PM.png】  | 【24†Image: Screen_Shot_2021-07-06_at_6.20.52_PM.png】  | 【25†Image: Screen_Shot_2021-07-06_at_6.21.01_PM.png】  | 【26†Image: Screen_Shot_2021-07-06_at_6.21.09_PM.png】\nL48: #### 2. Assign from the Class Report\nL49: \nL50: Go to the Students tab and select Class Reports. Switch to the Class Reports: All Progress option. Lessons are listed on the left side. Open each section until you see options for Main, Practice, and Basic. From there, you can tap Main, Practice 1, Practice 2, Basic, or the lesson title to assign to students.\nL51: \nL52: 【27†Image: Assign_ClassReport.png】\nL53: The All Progress report is intended to show a sequence of lessons that will teach toward each listed skill. Use the filters to change the subject to Math, ELA, or Logic+. If you’d like to see all the domains within a subject, use the small arrows to collapse the fields. In the image below, you’ll see 1st grade ELA domains: Reading Foundational Skills, Language, Reading Literature, and Reading Informational Texts.\nL54: \nL55: 【28†Image: ClassReport_Domain_1st_2.png】\nL56: Tap the arrow next to Reading Foundational Skills to see sub-domains like Capitalization & Sentence Parts and Short & Long Vowels.\nL57: \nL58: 【29†Image: ClassReport_Domain_1st_arrow2.png】  | 【30†Image: Subdomains2.png】\nL59: There are skills listed under each sub-domain, like Capitalization and Sentence Parts. The Capitalization skill only has one lesson, so you can tap Capitalization to assign. The skill Sentence Parts has an arrow next to it, meaning there are lessons within that skill. Tap Sentence Parts to find Main, Practice 1, Practice 2, and Basic lessons. Tap the word Main, Practice 1, Practice 2, or Basic to assign.\nL60: \nL61: 【31†Image: Skills2.png】  | 【32†Image: OpenLessons2.png】\nL62: ####\nL63: \nL64: #### 3. Go to the Search tab to find lessons by standard\nL65: \nL66: Use the dropdown menu to select the set of standards that is applicable to you. Continue progressing through the menu until you find the standard you’re looking for. If you would like to see a larger grouping of standards, you can select the (ALL) option from the dropdown menu. Tap directly on any lesson thumbnail to assign.\nL67: \nL68: 【33†Image: Assign_StandardSearch.png】\nL69: ## How to send assignments to students\nL70: \nL71: When you find a lesson you want to assign, tap the lesson thumbnail. Or, if you find a lesson in the Class Report, tap Main/Practice/Basic. You will see the following assignment dialog pop up.\nL72: \nL73: 【17†Image: AssignDialog.png】\nL74: If you’d like to play through the lesson before assigning, tap Preview in the top left corner. You can fast forward through the lesson if you enable Fast-Forward Button in Teacher Settings. Select the students who should receive the lesson. Change the Date to the day you’d like the assignment to appear on student devices.\nL75: \nL76: 【34†Image: AssignDialog_Preview.png】  | 【35†Image: AssignDialog_Date.png】\nL77: Be sure to tap Save! Students will receive the assignment on the date you selected. When they open the app, they’ll see a ❤️ next to their Library. The ❤️ tells them they have assignments waiting for them from their teacher!\nL78: \nL79: 【36†Image: AssignDialog_Save.png】  | 【37†Image: Assignment_Heart.png】\nL80: ## How to manage existing assignments\nL81: \nL82: You can manage existing assignments from the Assignments tab or from the Assignments class report.\nL83: \nL84: To manage from the Assignments tab, select Assignments at the top of the screen. You’ll see assignments organized by date. There is a fraction bubble next to each assignment that indicates the number of students who completed the assignment.\nL85: \nL86: 【38†Image: AssignmentsTab.png】\nL87: The Future Assignments section shows assignments that are scheduled for a future date. The Current Assignments section shows the assignments that students currently see in their view. The Archived Assignments section shows assignments that were sent to students in the past. Assignments are automatically archived after 2 weeks. You can change the archive interval in your Teacher Settings.\nL88: From the Assignments tab, you can delete assignments. Tap Delete Assignments, and you will see small “x” buttons appear. Tap the x buttons to delete individual lessons, or an entire day’s worth of lessons.\nL89: \nL90: 【39†Image: DeleteAssignments_Button.png】  | 【40†Image: DeleteAssignments.png】\nL91: \nL92: \nL93: \nL94: You can also edit assignments from the Assignments tab. Tap the fraction bubble next to any lesson thumbnail. This will take you to the Assignments report.\nL95: 【41†Image: FractionBubble.png】  | 【42†Image: Report_Assignments.png】\nL96: \nL97: \nL98: \nL99: From here, you can tap a lesson thumbnail to bring up the Assign dialog. This is where you can edit the date and the students who received the assignment. Be sure to tap Save to confirm any changes.\nL100: \nL101: 【43†Image: Report_Assignments2.png】  | 【44†Image: AssignDialog.png】\nL102: \nL103: \nL104: \nL105: Now you know the ins and outs of assigning lessons!\nL106: \nL107: Was this article helpful?\nL108: \nL109: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL110: \nL111: 10 out of 12 found this helpful\nL112: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL113: \nL114: 【45†Return to top】\nL115: ## Comments\nL116: \nL117: 0 comments\nL118: \nL119: Article is closed for comments.\nL120: \nL121: 【46†Khan Academy】\nL122: \nL123: 【47†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFAQ: How do I assign lessons by standard? – Khan Academy (https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042197971)\nciteturn1027view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1025view5\",\"id\":28}); Redirected to URL: https://khankids.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360042197971-FAQ-How-do-I-assign-lessons-by-standard; Total lines: 60\nL0: 【0†Skip to main content】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Submit a request】\nL3: \nL4: [Input][Input] [Input: Search]\nL5: \nL6: Articles in this section\nL7:   * 【2†Our Accessibility Statement】\nL8:   * 【3†Five ways to use Khan Kids for back to school success】\nL9:   * 【4†Quick start guide for preschool through 2nd grade teachers】\nL10:   * 【5†✨ NEW: Teacher Dashboard on the web】\nL11:   * 【6†✨ NEW: Manage student access to areas of the app】\nL12:   * 【7†Module 1: Setting up a Class Account】\nL13:   * 【8†Learning Topics: Using Khan Academy Kids in Educational Settings】\nL14:   * 【9†Module 2: Using Class Codes】\nL15:   * 【10†Daily Schedules for Ages 2-8】\nL16:   * 【11†Module 3: Assigning lessons】\nL17: 【12†See more】\nL18: # FAQ: How do I assign lessons by standard?\nL19: \nL20:   * February 26, 2026 23:44\nL21:   * Updated\nL22: \nL23: Khan Academy Kids is developed alongside experts from Stanford University, and is aligned with several sets of educational standards. If you teach to Common Core State Standards or to the Head Start Early Learning Outcomes Framework, you can now search by standard to find related lessons.\nL24: \nL25: 1. Open the app and tap your teacher avatar. Enter your password. Your teacher view will open on the Students tab.\nL26: 【13†Image: StudentTab.png】\nL27: \nL28: \nL29: \nL30: 2. Go to the Search tab. You will see a dropdown menu that says Choose Standard. Tap the dropdown menu and select the set of standards that is applicable to you.\nL31: \nL32: 【14†Image: StandardSearch.png】\nL33: \nL34: Note: Our “KHAN” standards cover some early math topics and executive functioning skills. These standards are based on the Sesame Street Framework for School Readiness and guidelines from Harvard University’s Center on the Developing Child Harvard.\nL35: 3. After selecting your set of standards, the menu will ask you to select a domain. You will then see standards strands (CCSS) or sub-domains (ELOF), and the menu will continue to carry you down to the individual standards.\nL36:   * At any point in the menu, you can select \"BACK\" to return to the previous drop-down options.\nL37:   * If you would like to see a larger grouping of standards, you can select the (ALL) option from the drop-down menu. For example, if you would like to browse through the 1st Grade Common Core Geometry standards, you can navigate to: Common Core 1st Grade > CCSS.MATH > CCSS.MATH.1.G > CCSS.MATH.1.G (ALL).\nL38: 4. As you browse by standard, you can assign lessons by tapping into the lesson. For further instructions, please see, 【15†Module 3: Assigning Lessons】.\nL39: \nL40: \nL41: \nL42: Was this article helpful?\nL43: \nL44: [Button: Yes] [Button: No]\nL45: \nL46: 6 out of 8 found this helpful\nL47: \nL48: Have more questions? 【1†Submit a request】\nL49: \nL50: 【16†Return to top】\nL51: ## Comments\nL52: \nL53: 0 comments\nL54: \nL55: Article is closed for comments.\nL56: \nL57: 【17†Khan Academy】\nL58: \nL59: 【18†Powered by Zendesk†www.zendesk.com】\n"
